      "worked_solution": "We count the number of rectangles. We see that there are $3$ rectangles.\n\nWe count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $6$ shapes in total.\n\nSo the ratio of rectangles to total shapes is $3:6.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers in a ratio by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,3 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,6 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of rectangles to the total shapes is $1:2.$",
